quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  8,41,"And know that whatever you take (legitimately) as spoils of war, a fifth of it is for Allah and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and (his) close relatives, the orphans, the needy and the travellers if you believe in Allah and what We sent down to Our (exalted) Servant on the Day of Distinction, the day when the two armies encountered (each other on the battlefield of Badr). And Allah is All-Capable of everything."
  8,42,"And (remember) when you were on the nearer bank (of the valley towards Medina), and they (i.e. the army of the Meccans) were on the farther bank (of the valley), and the (mercantile) caravan (of Abu Sufyan) was in a lower place than you. Had you mutually made an appointment (to fight), you would have surely reached there at different times (but Allah coincided your encounter)—so that Allah might conclude a matter which was bound to be fulfilled, (and) that whoever perishes should perish with clear evidence, and whoever survives should survive with clear evidence. And Allah is indeed All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
  8,43,"And (remember) when Allah showed them (i.e. the enemy troops) to you in your dream as being few. Had He shown them to you as being many, you would have surely lost hope and disputed about the matter (of war), but Allah saved (you from being disheartened). Indeed, He is the All-Knowing of what is in the breasts."
  8,44,"And (also remember) when He made them appear to you, at the time of your encounter, to be few in your eyes, and He made you appear to be few in their eyes, so that Allah may conclude a matter that was bound to be done. And to Allah, all matters are returned."
  8,45,"O believers! When you face a troop (in battle), stand firm and remember Allah frequently so that you may prosper."
